{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"bovine-sagacious-vole","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Class\n\nIn job `100874330553`:\n\n- **5 × `UnicodeDecodeError: 'charmap' codec can't decode byte 0x8f in position 1332: character maps\n  to <undefined>`**\n- **2 × `UnicodeDecodeError: 'utf-8' codec can't decode byte 0x97 in position 45: invalid start\n  byte`**\n\n`charmap` is cp1252, Windows' default locale codec. rebar reads files and subprocess output in text\nmode without an explicit `encoding=`, so Python picks the locale codec on Windows and UTF-8\nelsewhere. Byte `0x8f` is unmapped in cp1252, so the read raises outright.\n\nThe second variant is the mirror image: output that is *not* UTF-8 (a Windows tool emitting cp1252,\nor UTF-16 — the log also contains an `AssertionError` whose text reads\n`W^@i^@n^@d^@o^@w^@s^@ ^@S^@u^@b^@s^@y^@s^@t^@e^@m^@…`, i.e. UTF-16LE read as bytes) being decoded\nas UTF-8.\n\n## What the fix must decide\n\nTwo separate rules, and conflating them is how this class recurs:\n\n1. **Files rebar owns** (the event log, snapshots, config) are UTF-8 by contract — pass\n   `encoding=\"utf-8\"` explicitly at every `open()`. `PYTHONUTF8=1` in CI would mask this rather than\n   fix it for users, so fix the call sites.\n2. **Output from foreign processes** (`git`, `wsl`, external tools) has an encoding rebar does not\n   control. Decode with an explicit codec and an explicit error policy\n   (`errors=\"replace\"` for diagnostics), never with the locale default.\n\n## Blocked by S1\n\n## Proving command\n\n```\nuv run --no-sync pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -q -p no:cacheprovider 2>&1 \\\n  | grep -c \"UnicodeDecodeError\"   # must be 0\n```\non `windows-latest`, plus a lint-level proof so it cannot regress: an AST scan asserting no\n`open(...)` in `src/rebar` omits `encoding=` in text mode (the repo already runs whole-tree AST\npolicy scans in pytest, so this belongs alongside them).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Zero `UnicodeDecodeError` in a Windows sweep.\n2. A scan test fails if a new text-mode `open()` without `encoding=` is added under `src/rebar`.\n","id":"fc16-8271-b85b-4b10","parent_id":"55da-cee1-e556-4735","priority":3,"tags":["windows","portability","encoding"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"S7: the cp1252 console codec cannot decode subprocess output — 7 UnicodeDecodeErrors"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788571397989731413,"uuid":"1fc4171e-dc17-4b95-a2d9-26fa6766a704"}